      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2e0a4e8464150716ffd322|full_name}: Okay, with that I have repro'd it. Unfortunately, this is not fixable on our end. I am not actually sure why this works on the face mirror, potentially because it renders on the stacked UI camera. However, this is strictly a shader issue on the avatar.\n\nIn technical terms, part of the face is rendered with an alpha value not set to pure 1.0, most likely due to the alpha blend options you mention. There is no workaround for this, since as far as the shader on the personal mirror is concerned, this is the exact same as real transparency on your avatar, which *should* blend with the background. The only time we apply a workaround is when `color.a == 0 && any(color.rgb)` - it's fixed with just `any(color.rgb)`, but as I said, this would break all transparency on the mirror entirely.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
