  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-03-12T05:26:15.745Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If you mask out the environment in your personal mirror set, there's transparency issues similar to [those that occur with the face mirror.](https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1801-face-mirror-with-transparency-results-in-transparency-issues-with-some-avat)\n\nThese issues are much easier to notice with a fully opaque personal mirror and a contrasting/bright background. (See attached image for white \"Artifacting\" across the face)\n\nRunefox discovered that this issue appears with poiyomi if the material was a different rendering mode originally then set to opaque. Resetting Alpha Destination Blend to `OneMinusSrcAlpha `and Alpha Blend Op to `Max` solves alpha issues in the face mirror AND the personal mirror. \n\nIf a solution was found for the face mirror and was also applicable to the personal mirror, it'd be neat to see that applied.",
